\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Tool and sandbox interaction}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{agent}
\tag{tool-use}

\p{A \strong{tool interaction} is an action whose environment transition
invokes an external operation and returns its result as an observation. A
\strong{sandbox} is an environment that isolates such operations and records
the resources and state changes they are permitted to cause.}

\p{ReAct interleaves language reasoning with external actions; see
\citef{yao2023react}, Sections 2--3. Software-agent systems instantiate the
same interface with repositories, shells, tests, and browsers. FTIP adopts the
interface but treats its security policy, state reset, and execution cost as
part of the environment specification.}

\p{A sandbox can produce high-quality evidence, such as a passing test suite.
It can also expose shortcuts or nondeterministic failures. The verifier and
the environment therefore remain separate even when they run in the same
container.}
